{
  "_doc": "Class outfits for Chibi 2 (2026-09-25). An OUTFIT is only the clothes, the headwear and the carried items — no face, no body — so any game can dress any body as any class: `dressAs(avatar, outfit)` in avatar-3d/js/class-outfits.js lays these slots over an avatar and leaves the rest alone. Keys are the Emberveil/Farhold class ids. `held`/`offhand` are what the class LOOKS like it carries in a portrait; a game that equips real items (Farhold) draws its own hands. Every id here exists in avatar-2d/js/parts (chibi2-parts.js registers the Chibi 2-only ones), so the shared normaliser keeps them. Classes a player asked to be distinct: the horned helm is the FIGHTER's alone; warrior, knight, paladin, runesmith, druid, shaman and tactician each have their own headwear.",
